  "rationale": "A held MIDI note stored its channel and step but not its song. Release after an automatic song transition read the new song channel for length quantisation and queued the completed length into the new song. Store the onset song and use it for release lookup and event ownership. Final chord release still determines the shared length.",
  "oracle": "README.md:239: recorded lengths and chords use the active onset step; shared chord length is first press to final release. A 300 ms hold at 100 BPM is two sixteenth steps, replaying as 1/3 second at 90 BPM. Both note and staggered chord cases assert MIDI note-on placement and note-off durations across three cycles. Cross-song ownership is characterisation, not manual text.",
